course: dictionary
lesson: 10631
title: Unfriendly: people, places and words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unfriendly means not kind or welcoming, not wanting to be nice to other people. It is built from friendly with un- in front, so it means the opposite of friendly.
explain: «The wood is cold, dark and unfriendly: night-jars rattle, an owl brushes his shoulder.» Here unfriendly describes a place that is hard and not safe, not a person who is unkind. The clues around it, cold, dark and startling noises, tell you what it means.
explain: Someone who seems unfriendly may just be shy or new. «Someone who is quiet may be shy or new, not unfriendly.» Look at the whole situation before you decide what a word means about a person.
fact: Unfriendly is an adjective, so it describes a noun: an unfriendly stranger, an unfriendly dog, an unfriendly place.
fact: «Unfriendly» means not kind or welcoming.
fact: «Unfriendly» can also describe a place or thing that is hard or not safe, like an unfriendly climate.
fact: Friendly is the opposite of unfriendly.
fact: In compounds, «-unfriendly» means bad for something: «environment-unfriendly» and «user-unfriendly».
exercise: «The wood is cold, dark and unfriendly.» Here unfriendly describes the wood. What does it mean? | Full of friendly animals waving hello | *Hard and not safe | Warm and cosy | Very loud and busy
exercise: Mia says the quiet new girl is unfriendly. What else might be true? | She cannot speak English | She wants to be unkind to everyone | She is rude and thinks she is better than others | *She may be shy or new
exercise: «User-unfriendly» is said about a computer game. What does it mean? | Friendly to every user | Very quick and clever | *Hard for users to understand and use | Good for the environment
test: What is the opposite of unfriendly? | Hard | Unkind | *Friendly | Shy
test: «An unfriendly dog may growl or show its teeth, so keep away.» What should you do? | *Keep away from it | Give it your sandwich | Pat it on the head | Call it closer
exam: Ben says, «The climate here is unfriendly for plants.» What does Ben mean? | Plants are friendly and welcome | *The conditions are hard for plants to live in | Plants make a lot of noise | Plants grow best when they are ignored
